// A colony creature (Reports/creature-direction.md). `kind: Creature`, so
// the CA sweep never moves it -- `creature.rs` relocates the whole chain
// explicitly from the active-site schedule, exactly as it does the worm.
//
// Flammable on the same terms as everything else, which is the entire
// reason a burning nest needs no code: fire.rs applies uniformly from these
// numbers alone, an ant burns into `corpse`, and a corpse is food. The loop
// closes itself.
//
// Dark, and deliberately not red: an ant is one or two cells at play zoom
// against soil and sand, and the readable signal at that size is contrast
// against the ground rather than hue. Three shades so a column of them does
// not read as a drawn line.
(
    name: "ant",
    display: "Ant",
    kind: Creature,
    density: 1.0,
    colors: [
        (38, 30, 28),
        (52, 42, 38),
        (28, 22, 20),
    ],
    flammability: 0.6,
    burn_temperature: 500.0,
    burn_duration: 40,
    burns_into: "corpse",
    heat_conductivity: 0.1,
)
